// cmd/dql-lsp is its own module so the library stays dependency-free: the
// server needs a JSON-RPC stack, and nothing importing DQL should inherit it.
//
// That module used to reach the library through `replace ... => ../..`, which
// made `go install github.com/xraph/dql/cmd/dql-lsp@latest` impossible — the
// go command refuses to install a module carrying a replace directive, so the
// documented way to obtain the server did not work at all.
//
// This workspace does the same job without that cost. Inside the repository
// the server builds against the library beside it, so `make test` exercises
// local changes; outside it, the module's own require line applies and the
// server installs normally.
go 1.26.0

use (
	.
	./cmd/dql-lsp
)
